---
title: "Sale Lifecycle State Machine (LegionFixedPriceSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_initialized: initialize()
    q_initialized --> q_prefund: block.timestamp >= prefundStartTime
    q_prefund --> q_allocation: block.timestamp > prefundEndTime
    q_allocation --> q_active: block.timestamp >= startTime
    q_active --> q_refund: block.timestamp > endTime
    q_refund --> q_results: block.timestamp > refundEndTime
    q_results --> q_supply: publishSaleResults()
    q_supply --> q_distribution: supplyTokens()
    q_distribution --> [*]: all claims settled

    q_initialized --> q_canceled: cancel()
    q_prefund --> q_canceled: cancel()
    q_allocation --> q_canceled: cancel()
    q_active --> q_canceled: cancel()
    q_refund --> q_canceled: cancel()
    q_results --> q_canceled: cancel() (before publishSaleResults)
    q_canceled --> [*]: all investors withdraw via withdrawInvestedCapitalIfCanceled

    note right of q_prefund
        INV-001: Phases are strictly sequential and time-ordered
        INV-002: Cancel is possible from any phase before results publication
        INV-003: Prefund period 1 hour to 12 weeks
        INV-004: Active sale period 1 hour to 12 weeks
        INV-005: Refund period 1 to 2 weeks
        INV-006: Allocation processing period 1 to 2 weeks (off-chain)
    end note

    note right of q_distribution
        INV-007: Token distribution requires both results published AND tokens supplied
        INV-008: Project can withdraw capital only after supplying tokens
    end note
